attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a spine.** Columns 0 to 7, `degS` to `sspB`, are carried by 96 to 100% of chromosomes, all persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0% of calls {S1}. The model names 98 to 100% of them, fewest at column 6, `sspA`, 98% {S1}.

@variable **A single variable column breaks the first spine**: column 8, `dcuC`, shell, carried by 83% {S2.c8}. Then the `nan` genes, columns 9 to 14, [[n-acetylneuraminate catabolism]], carried by 95 to 96% {S3, Q}. At column 15, `yhcG`, a fork column carried by 58%, the most plastic stretch of the window, RGP 35% {S4, P}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 97 against 94%, and hesitates less there, 0.07 against 0.27 bits {M}. It hesitates most at column 15, `yhcG`, a fork column, 0.89 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends on fork and variable columns.** Columns 75 to 79, `yhbO` to `diaA`, are carried by 52 to 66% of chromosomes, all persistent {S8}. The last column is `diaA`, in 52% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 97% of genes**, 0.09 bits on average, perplexity 1.2 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 1.10 against 0.06 bits, and names fewer genes, 57% against 98% {C}.

